# CORE

## Version

0.15

---

# 🎯 Project Identity

Intuition is a:

```text
supportable deterministic cognitive training product
```

built around:

* explicit ownership
* bounded contexts
* deterministic gameplay runtime
* explainable analytics
* deployment-oriented architecture

The project intentionally prioritizes:

```text
supportability over theoretical elegance
```

and:

```text
explicit ownership over generalized abstraction
```

---

# 🧠 Core Philosophy

The system is designed around:

```text
small explicit bounded systems
```

instead of:

```text
implicit orchestration frameworks
```

The architecture intentionally avoids:

* hidden lifecycle coordination
* generalized runtime engines
* adaptive orchestration graphs
* mega-context environments
* cross-cutting runtime ownership

---

# 🧩 Bounded Contexts

## Gameplay

Responsible for:

* deterministic runtime
* reducer lifecycle
* round generation
* gameplay semantics
* session progression

Gameplay does NOT own:

* persistence orchestration
* analytics
* renderer infrastructure
* profile lifecycle
* telemetry

---

## Statistics

Responsible for:

* observational analytics
* reconstruction-based insights
* transforms
* trend analysis
* selection-driven exploration

Statistics are:

```text
read-only observational systems
```

Statistics MUST NOT:

* influence gameplay runtime
* affect reducers
* inject adaptive difficulty
* mutate gameplay lifecycle

---

## Profile

Responsible for:

* identity
* profile persistence
* active profile runtime state
* parent/child structure
* PIN security
* recovery state

Profile subsystem is intentionally separated into:

| Responsibility               | Owner              |
| ---------------------------- | ------------------ |
| profile persistence          | ProfileRepository  |
| runtime active profile state | ProfileManager     |
| runtime synchronization      | ProfileRuntime     |
| bootstrap lifecycle          | ProfileInitializer |
| UI lifecycle                 | ProfileViewModel   |

The profile subsystem intentionally avoids:

* orchestration responsibilities
* application-wide coordination
* telemetry ownership
* capability orchestration
* generalized identity runtime

---

## Rendering

Responsible for:

* visual projection
* renderer semantics
* resource interpretation
* notebook ownership
* stimulus presentation

Rendering does NOT own:

* gameplay semantics
* analytics
* profile state
* lifecycle coordination

---

## Markdown Explainability

Responsible for:

* help content
* localized explanations
* markdown dialogs
* semantic illustrations

Markdown subsystem is:

```text
passive and declarative
```

It is NOT:

* runtime orchestration
* feature coordination
* gameplay logic

---

# 🔄 Runtime Philosophy

The runtime architecture is:

```text
reducer-first
```

Gameplay lifecycle must remain:

* deterministic
* explicit
* bounded
* traceable
* supportable

The project intentionally avoids:

* orchestration engines
* generalized transition systems
* implicit runtime graphs
* distributed lifecycle ownership

---

# 🧱 Persistence Philosophy

Persistence layers are intentionally:

```text
boring bounded adapters
```

Repositories SHOULD:

* persist validated data
* expose storage queries
* remain runtime-agnostic

Repositories MUST NOT:

* orchestrate runtime lifecycle
* mutate gameplay state
* coordinate subsystems
* own telemetry
* perform hidden synchronization

Runtime synchronization must remain:

```text
explicit
```

and visible in:

* bootstrap layers
* runtime boundaries
* UI lifecycle owners

---

# 🚀 Bootstrap Philosophy

Application bootstrap must remain:

* explicit
* deterministic
* bounded
* sequentially understandable

Bootstrap layers are responsible for:

* persistence initialization
* runtime restoration
* explicit synchronization

Bootstrap layers are NOT:

* orchestration engines
* generalized lifecycle coordinators

---

# 🔒 Security Philosophy

Security systems are isolated bounded contexts.

They are responsible for:

* PIN hashing
* recovery state
* failed attempt tracking
* parent profile protection

Security systems MUST remain isolated from:

* gameplay runtime
* analytics
* renderer infrastructure

---

# 📊 Analytics Philosophy

Analytics are reconstruction-based.

The project intentionally prefers:

```text
derive insights from persisted runtime records
```

instead of:

```text
opaque cached aggregate systems
```

This improves:

* explainability
* determinism
* supportability
* auditability

---

# ⚠️ Explicitly Avoided Directions

The project intentionally freezes or avoids:

* orchestration runtime frameworks
* generalized process engines
* adaptive gameplay AI
* opaque scoring systems
* universal lifecycle coordinators
* implicit subsystem synchronization
* mega-context environments

These directions are considered high-risk for:

* ownership erosion
* lifecycle coupling
* supportability collapse
* debugging paralysis
* implicit relationship explosion

---

# 🧠 Architectural Risk Awareness

The project continuously monitors risks of:

## Ownership Erosion

When subsystems begin to:

```text
know a little about everything
```

---

## Implicit Relationship Explosion

Especially dangerous in:

* capability systems
* orchestration remnants
* profile lifecycle
* telemetry integration
* adaptive runtime systems

---

## Lifecycle Coupling

When:

* UI
* telemetry
* analytics
* persistence

begin influencing gameplay runtime semantics.

---

## Mega-Context Growth

Especially dangerous for:

* AppContainer
* environment systems
* profile runtime
* capability infrastructure

---

# 🎯 Product Direction

The project is intentionally transitioning from:

```text
experimental architecture playground
```

toward:

```text
supportable long-term product
```

The architectural priority is now:

* bounded ownership
* deterministic lifecycle
* deployment safety
* supportability
* explainability
* maintainability

instead of:

* maximal abstraction
* theoretical generalization
* framework experimentation

---

# ✅ Core Architectural Principles

## Explicit ownership

Every subsystem must have:

* clear boundaries
* clear lifecycle ownership
* clear responsibilities

---

## Explicit synchronization

Runtime synchronization must remain:

```text
visible and intentional
```

not hidden inside repositories or infrastructure.

---

## Deterministic runtime

Gameplay semantics must remain:

* reproducible
* traceable
* bounded
* testable

---

## Supportability-first architecture

Architectural decisions are evaluated primarily by:

* debuggability
* maintainability
* bounded complexity
* lifecycle clarity
* operational supportability

---

# 📌 Strategic Position

Version 0.15 represents the transition point where the project:

stops optimizing for:

```text
architectural experimentation
```

and begins optimizing for:

```text
long-term supportable evolution
```

